Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.1998016Z Language versions, standards of one's own, a comment language and concrete syntax trees by default.
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.1998439Z 
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.1998933Z - `formatMeta` shows the meta program as Links Notation, so the meta language of any text can be seen.
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.1999693Z - Every language has a single entry with versions:
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2000227Z   - programming languages have major versions (`python@2`);
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2001386Z   - natural languages have regional spellings (British English, chosen from the browser languages), smaller vocabularies down to the semantic primes, and controlled standards.
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2002285Z - The 65 semantic primes are given for every supported natural language, as a `minimal-<language>` version of each.
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2003212Z - Every word of a language's vocabulary can be changed and saved as a version of one's own (`languageVocabulary`, `vocabularyChanges`, `writeLanguageVersion`, `loadLanguageVersion`). Every changed word takes effect.
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2004445Z - Word standards hold up to 1024 words. New words are defined through the words a standard already has, recursively, with Wikidata lookups through a cache and an offline pre-cache (`createStandard`, `defineWord`, `wikidataLookup`).
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2005322Z - Comments can be translated into another natural language apart from the code (`commentLanguage`).
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2005820Z - Whitespace and comments are kept as written:
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2006349Z   - the spaces inside comments;
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2006740Z   - empty lines between statements and between functions, or the lack of them;
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2007128Z   - trailing comments;
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2007399Z   - comments that close an indented block.
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2007713Z - The web demo:
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2007988Z   - shows the meta language of both texts;
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2008381Z   - translates the right text into a newly chosen left language instead of failing;
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2008835Z   - generates random Program, Function and Statement examples;
Check for Changesets	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T10:44:25.2009441Z   - has a Standards tab and a settings panel built on link-foundation/ui with themes, skins and seven interface languages.
